---
// Refund Policy. The rule mirrors docs/release-and-licensing.md (Sales) and
// must match the refund setting in the Lemon Squeezy store.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Marker from '../components/Marker.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="When and how you can get a refund for a Pocket License."
>
  <section class="container page">
    <Marker shape="square" play />
    <h1 class="h indent">Refund Policy</h1>
    <div class="indent prose">
    <p class="label muted">Last updated: November 13, 2026</p>

    <p>
      Pocket has a 3-day Trial with every feature, so you can check that it suits you before
      you pay. If you bought a License and changed your mind, here is how refunds work.
    </p>

    <h2>When you can get a refund</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You ask within 14 days of your purchase, and</li>
      <li>your License key was never activated.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      After an Activation the sale is final. Removing the Activation later does not change
      this.
    </p>

    <h2>How to ask</h2>
    <p>
      Write to <a href="mailto:dk2la@icloud.com">dk2la@icloud.com</a> and include your order
      number or the email address you used at checkout. You don't need to give a reason.
    </p>

    <h2>How you are refunded</h2>
    <p>
      Refunds are made through Lemon Squeezy, our merchant of record, to the payment method you
      used for the purchase. How long the money takes to arrive depends on your bank or card
      provider. Once a refund is made, the License key stops working.
    </p>

    <h2>If something doesn't work</h2>
    <p>
      If Pocket doesn't work properly on your Mac, write to the same address, even after an
      Activation or after the 14 days. We will try to fix the problem.
    </p>

    <h2>Your legal rights</h2>
    <p>
      This policy does not limit rights that the law gives you and that cannot be waived, such
      as consumer rights in your country of residence. Where those rights go further than this
      policy, they apply.
    </p>

    <p>See also the <a href="/terms">Terms</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
